  "text": "A place where bread and cakes are made or sold.\n\nHelp Pip bring new stories to Grandma’s garden.\n\nUp to this time, or despite what was just said.\n\nA place beside the water where a boat can stop.\n\nOne or more, without choosing a particular one.\n\nthe memory of the people sharing stories today.\n\nIdentifies or asks about one of several things.\n\nTell Grandma why Mara has been unable to visit.\n\nMeet the SparkFest crew, Loop, Pip and Grandma.\n\nA group of words expressing a complete thought.\n\nEquipment with steps used to climb up or down.\n\nMade a series of quick, light knocking sounds.\n\nUpright supports at the sides of the crossing.\n\nOne person or thing, without naming which one.\n\nA way from one side of the river to the other.\n\nWhat about the people waiting for their bread?\n\nSomething you remember about an earlier event.\n\nBad weather with strong wind, rain or thunder.\n\nExisting, happening, or in a particular state.\n\nA room or building where people do their work.\n\nYou guide Pip · Rina and Sol do their own work\n\nM-17-71q-3-19 17-18 19 1 17 18L8-80q-13 9-25 9\n\nPeople who buy things from a shop or business.\n\nCreate something or cause something to happen.\n\nA flat container used to carry or bake things.\n\nThe garden keeps the stories that were shared.\n\nReading help · Loop is waiting at this picture\n\nConnects something with its result or purpose.\n\nMoving toward something to touch or get to it.\n\nThe wooden bridge pieces are beside the river.\n\nNew things that people have designed and made.\n\nPieces of information sent or told to someone.\n\nDid the storm make Mara and Sol stop visiting?\n\nPut something more with what is already there.\n\nRelease that section’s rope before turning it.\n\nA short time or a particular part of an event.\n\nNoises that can be heard, or seems when heard.",
